sequenceDiagram
    title SPay UPI Payment With Redis, Idempotency, Outbox, Kafka
    participant Client as Flutter / Swagger
    participant API as Payment API
    participant Redis
    participant DB as PostgreSQL
    participant Simulator
    participant Publisher as Outbox Publisher
    participant Kafka
    participant Consumer as Kafka Consumer

    Client->>API: POST /api/payments/upi + X-Idempotency-Key
    API->>DB: Check idempotency key and request hash
    alt Existing same request
        DB-->>API: Stored response
        API-->>Client: Same payment response, no double debit
    else New request
        API->>Redis: Check payment rate limit
        API->>DB: Resolve sender and receiver UPI handles
        API->>Redis: Acquire sender account lock
        API->>DB: Validate PIN, account state, balance
        API->>Simulator: Decide success, retryable failure, or final failure
        alt Success
            API->>DB: Debit sender, credit receiver, ledger, timeline
            API->>DB: Save outbox event PAYMENT_SUCCEEDED
        else Retryable failure
            API->>DB: Save attempts, timeline, DLQ, outbox event
        else Non-retryable failure
            API->>DB: Save failed payment, attempt, outbox event
        end
        API->>DB: Save idempotency response
        API->>Redis: Release sender account lock
        API-->>Client: Final payment response
    end

    loop Every 5 seconds
        Publisher->>DB: Read pending or failed outbox events
        Publisher->>Kafka: Publish payment event envelope
        Publisher->>DB: Mark outbox event PUBLISHED
    end

    Kafka-->>Consumer: Deliver payment event
    Consumer->>DB: Store processed event if not already consumed
